scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: firefly
run_id: 6
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 18
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 48.6
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: \"from_file_or_default swallows parse errors\
    \ silently \u2014 config.rs:77-79 \u2014 unwrap_or_default() meaning a malformed\
    \ TOML file silently falls back to defaults.\""
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented sanitized Display on CliError \u2014 error.rs:49 ServerError\
    \ shows generic message. Reviewer verified: \"CWE-209 error exposure is properly\
    \ mitigated.\" However, reviewer also flagged NotFound variant as leaking inner\
    \ string, so partial catch. The core CWE-209 mitigation was implemented but not\
    \ comprehensively."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests (CRLF rejection) and Dev implemented\
    \ HeaderValue::from_str() which rejects CRLF. But the finding is about tenant_id\
    \ being a raw String instead of using axiathon-core's validated TenantId type.\
    \ No phase flagged the type-safety gap \u2014 only the CRLF injection vector was\
    \ addressed."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer flagged a toml version mismatch (0.8 vs 0.9) but did not flag
    that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true. The
    deps were added to [workspace.dependencies] but the crate Cargo.toml uses direct
    versions rather than workspace references.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: "RawConfig uses #[derive(Deserialize)]
    without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. Operator typos like servre_url are silently
    ignored." Also noted token fields are silently dropped. This directly addresses
    the silent-ignore-unknown-fields concern.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ... always passes when first branch is true). TEA wrote the test with this flaw,
    Dev didn't fix it, Reviewer didn't catch the test logic error.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    via `let _ = config`. TEA wrote it, Dev passed it, Reviewer did not flag the test
    quality issue.
